                <pb facs="0627" n="585" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg585"/>

                <head>[Extract.]</head>
                <p>“During our stay the Wachusett slipped her cable, at midnight of the 24th, and
                    followed an English steamer, called the Dolphin, to sea, and returned to the
                    port at 9 p.m. of the 25th. The Dolphin was on a voyage from England to Nassau,
                    and, I was informed by the acting British consul, was regularly entered and
                    cleared at the custom-house.”</p>
            </div>
